        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(signal): add setup wizard container flow",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a problem where Signal setup required manual native `signal-cli` configuration even when users wanted OpenClaw to help start and link a local Signal REST container. It also fixes setup/status gaps where Signal transport mode, receive readiness, and multi-account setup state could be misreported or persisted on the wrong account.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nSignal setup now owns its container, native, and existing-server setup paths inside the Signal plugin while core setup only gains the generic rollback result needed to avoid persisting failed setup attempts. The runtime can distinguish native and container Signal APIs, probe receive readiness, and persist per-account transport settings without moving Signal-specific behavior into core.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can configure Signal through the setup wizard with a Docker container flow, see QR/linking guidance, and get clearer status output when a Signal account is missing, unreachable, or receive streaming is unavailable. Existing Signal users can reconfigure server URLs without re-entering an already saved Signal number, and multi-account configs keep default transport fields scoped to the intended account.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Focused Signal setup validation: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/signal/src/setup-core.test.ts` passed, covering missing-account rejection and existing-account reconfiguration.\n- Signal setup/status/runtime slices passed across setup entry, config schema, client adapter, send/reaction, status, health, and channel setup wizard tests.\n- Plugin SDK export checks passed after adding the narrow `openclaw/plugin-sdk/qr-terminal-runtime` subpath.\n- Native review phase: clean on the final target.\n- Cold review phase: clean on the same final target.\n- Remote build: `node scripts/crabbox-wrapper.mjs run --provider blacksmith-testbox --id tbx_01kwwyt0m63bsz123rgyp7e7qe --timing-json --shell -- \"env CI=1 corepack pnpm build\"` passed on Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kwwyt0m63bsz123rgyp7e7qe`.\n- Safety: no real `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json` changes and no manual Signal messages were used for this proof.\n",
